Wire launch-at-login and recording sound cues

Two macOS features that existed only as inert settings flags are now real:

- Launch at login: ILaunchAtLoginService seam + RegistryLaunchAtLoginService
  (per-user HKCU Run key, no elevation). Applied on settings save and
  reconciled on startup so an externally-removed entry self-heals.
- Alert sounds: ISoundService seam + Win32SoundService (winmm PlaySound with
  system aliases, async/non-blocking). SoundController plays start/stop/ready/
  error cues from pipeline state, honoring the General > play sounds toggle.

DI exposes both in the real platform composition. Inner loop stays GREEN (175).

